    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.pick\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nis there an easy way to replace the folder/dir icons in mini.pick? also, one thing: I used a lot on fzf-lua and telescope, is there an easy way to add picker for user keymaps?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">is there an easy way to replace the folder/dir icons in mini.pick? also, one thing: I used a lot on fzf-lua and telescope, is there an easy way to add picker for user keymaps?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\nis there an easy way to replace the folder/dir icons in mini.pick? also, one thing: I used a lot on fzf-lua and telescope, is there an easy way to add picker for user keymaps?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-01-10T09:59:48Z",
    "comment_count": 2,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12143269?v=4",
                "login": "tjkuson",
                "resourcePath": "/tjkuson",
                "url": "https://github.com/tjkuson"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "I do\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal pick = require(\"mini.pick\")\r\npick.setup({ source = { show = pick.default_show } })\r\n```\r\n\r\nto disable icons as I couldn't find an option similar to mini.statusline's `show_icons`.\r\n\r\n",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I do</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local pick = require(&quot;mini.pick&quot;)\npick.setup({ source = { show = pick.default_show } })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">pick</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.pick<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">pick</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({ <span class=\"pl-smi\">source</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">show</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">pick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">default_show</span> } })</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">to disable icons as I couldn't find an option similar to mini.statusline's <code class=\"notranslate\">show_icons</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "I do\nlocal pick = require(\"mini.pick\")\npick.setup({ source = { show = pick.default_show } })\nto disable icons as I couldn't find an option similar to mini.statusline's show_icons.",
