        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "For reference, completely disabling icons [is documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/890db26e37bb28d8a95f05570dd0d9fa757b698b/doc/mini-pick.txt#L614-L618). Adjusting is done in similar way but with `show = function(buf_id, items, query) return MiniPick.default_show(buf_id, items, query, { show_icons = true, icons = { ... } }) end`. See [this part](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/890db26e37bb28d8a95f05570dd0d9fa757b698b/doc/mini-pick.txt#L971-L975) for relevant fields.\r\n\r\n> also, one thing: I used a lot on fzf-lua and telescope, is there an easy way to add picker for user keymaps?\r\n\r\nYou can use [`MiniExtra.pickers.keymaps`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/890db26e37bb28d8a95f05570dd0d9fa757b698b/doc/mini-extra.txt#L534) for that. Add `require('mini.extra').setup()` and call `:Pick keymaps`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">For reference, completely disabling icons <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/890db26e37bb28d8a95f05570dd0d9fa757b698b/doc/mini-pick.txt#L614-L618\">is documented</a>. Adjusting is done in similar way but with <code class=\"notranslate\">show = function(buf_id, items, query) return MiniPick.default_show(buf_id, items, query, { show_icons = true, icons = { ... } }) end</code>. See <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/890db26e37bb28d8a95f05570dd0d9fa757b698b/doc/mini-pick.txt#L971-L975\">this part</a> for relevant fields.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">also, one thing: I used a lot on fzf-lua and telescope, is there an easy way to add picker for user keymaps?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">You can use <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/890db26e37bb28d8a95f05570dd0d9fa757b698b/doc/mini-extra.txt#L534\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniExtra.pickers.keymaps</code></a> for that. Add <code class=\"notranslate\">require('mini.extra').setup()</code> and call <code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick keymaps</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "For reference, completely disabling icons is documented. Adjusting is done in similar way but with show = function(buf_id, items, query) return MiniPick.default_show(buf_id, items, query, { show_icons = true, icons = { ... } }) end. See this part for relevant fields.\n\nalso, one thing: I used a lot on fzf-lua and telescope, is there an easy way to add picker for user keymaps?\n\nYou can use MiniExtra.pickers.keymaps for that. Add require('mini.extra').setup() and call :Pick keymaps.",
